ORP diagnostic patch 09 — log silent mid-stream sample loss in the ALSA
TX path.

Context: operator reports audible glitches (e.g. the word "hundred" in
the PL report rendered as "h-dred", and similar with "repeater",
EchoLink traffic and CWID) that are NOT explained by any existing
svxlink warning, NOT a buffer underrun (svxlink-audio-monitor sees no
XRUN at the event), and NOT zerofill (svxlink keeps the codec buffer
full). Confirmed symptom: a chunk of samples vanishes from inside a
clip, the rest plays at normal speed.

Code-reading the TX chain (MsgHandler -> AudioFifo -> AudioPacer ->
AudioDeviceAlsa) shows MsgHandler correctly unreads on partial sink
writes (MsgHandler.cpp:505-508), the tx_fifo does NOT overwrite
(do_overwrite=false, no setOverwrite call), and AudioPacer
back-pressures. The one path that silently DROPS already-consumed
samples with no log is AudioDeviceAlsa::writeSpaceAvailable:

  - getBlocks() fills `buf`, advancing the upstream read pointers
    (samples are now CONSUMED from MsgHandler/FIFO/Pacer).
  - snd_pcm_writei() returns < 0 (typically -EPIPE = XRUN). The
    recovery (startPlayback + continue) throws `buf` away and
    re-pulls fresh samples on the next loop iteration. The
    consumed-but-unwritten frames are lost with no message. A brief
    XRUN that svxlink recovers from within one poll is also too fast
    for the 200 Hz audio-monitor to observe as an XRUN.
  - OR snd_pcm_writei() returns 0 <= n < frames_to_write (partial
    write). The existing "Audio was probably lost" warning covers
    this but never fires in practice (grep of /var/log/svxlink = 0),
    pointing at the < 0 XRUN-recover branch as the actual loss path.

This patch adds explicit, greppable log lines on BOTH loss paths with
cumulative frame counters, so events can be correlated with
operator-flagged audible glitches. Tag: "*** ORP-DIAG sample-loss:".
Logging only — no behaviour change. cerr is already captured in
/var/log/svxlink (the existing "Could not find audio clip" warning
uses cerr and appears there); <iostream> and snd_strerror are already
available in this translation unit.

--- src/async/audio/AsyncAudioDeviceAlsa.cpp.orig
+++ src/async/audio/AsyncAudioDeviceAlsa.cpp
@@ -512,6 +512,23 @@
     //       blocks_gotten, (int)frames_written);
     if (frames_written < 0)
     {
+      // ORP-DIAG patch 09: snd_pcm_writei failed (typically -EPIPE =
+      // XRUN). The frames in buf were already pulled by getBlocks()
+      // above, i.e. CONSUMED from the upstream chain (MsgHandler /
+      // AudioFifo / AudioPacer read pointers already advanced). The
+      // recovery below (startPlayback + continue) discards them with
+      // no retransmit -> silent mid-stream audio loss, exactly the
+      // "shorter word, rest at normal speed" symptom. Log every event.
+      static unsigned long long orp_xrun_lost_frames = 0;
+      if (frames_to_write > 0)
+      {
+        orp_xrun_lost_frames += frames_to_write;
+      }
+      cerr << "*** ORP-DIAG sample-loss: snd_pcm_writei(" << devName()
+           << ") err=" << frames_written << " ("
+           << snd_strerror(frames_written) << "); discarding "
+           << frames_to_write << " consumed frame(s); cum_xrun_lost="
+           << orp_xrun_lost_frames << "\n";
       if (!startPlayback(play_handle))
       {
         watch->setEnabled(false);
@@ -522,10 +539,20 @@

     if (frames_written != frames_to_write)
     {
-      cerr << "*** WARNING: Number of frames written to sound device "
-           << devName()
-           << " (" << frames_written << ") differs from what was expected ("
-           << frames_to_write << "). Audio was probably lost.\n";
+      // ORP-DIAG patch 09: partial write. buf was consumed from the
+      // upstream chain by getBlocks(); the unwritten remainder is
+      // dropped here (return) with no unread -> silent loss.
+      static unsigned long long orp_partial_lost_frames = 0;
+      int orp_lost = frames_to_write - frames_written;
+      if (orp_lost > 0)
+      {
+        orp_partial_lost_frames += orp_lost;
+      }
+      cerr << "*** ORP-DIAG sample-loss: partial snd_pcm_writei("
+           << devName() << ") wrote " << frames_written << " of "
+           << frames_to_write << "; lost " << orp_lost
+           << " consumed frame(s); cum_partial_lost="
+           << orp_partial_lost_frames << "\n";
       return;
     }

